      "problem": "Let $a=-2i-2j+4k$ and $b=2i-2j.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 0}{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\u27e80,0,0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
