      "knowledge_point": "Perpendicular Vectors",
      "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na\u22a5b\\,\u27f9\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot x \\\\  & =x-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ x-20 & =0 \\\\ x & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
